   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two key sounds",
     "texto": [
      "The group **sch** always sounds like a soft, continuous «sh»: **Tschüss** (bye), **Schmidt**, **schreibt** (writes), **Entschuldigung** (sorry).",
      "The combination **ch** has two pronunciations, depending on the vowel before it:",
      "1. **Ich-Laut** (soft): after **e, i** or a consonant, it sounds like a very soft «h» said with the tongue raised toward the roof of the mouth: **ich** (I), **mich** (me), **nicht** (not).",
      "2. **Ach-Laut** (hard): after **a, o, u**, it sounds further back in the throat, like the «ch» in Scottish «loch»: **auch** (also), **noch** (still, yet), **Nachname** (last name)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
